<!--
  Author: Jeroen Jonckheer
  Purpose: Workaround for NETSDK1050 raised by .NET 8 SDK when a net462
  cdsproj references a netstandard2.0 pcfproj without Visual Studio
  Build Tools installed.

  Reading the actual targets file at
  Microsoft.NET.Build.Extensions.NETFramework.targets, the offending
  error fires under three conditions:
    DependsOnNETStandard == true AND
    NETStandardInbox != true     AND
    _UsingOldSDK == true

  The pac-generated cdsproj uses the legacy non-SDK style (no
  <Project Sdk="..."> attribute), which sets _UsingOldSDK to true.

  We short-circuit the check by claiming the project does not depend on
  .NET Standard. This is safe because the cdsproj does not actually
  consume the referenced pcfproj's assembly - the PowerApps Solution
  targets only consume its content outputs (bundle.js, manifest, etc.)
  via a separate, SolutionPackager-driven pipeline.

  This file is implicitly imported by every project under the same
  directory tree (including pac-generated temporary wrappers under obj\).
-->
<Project>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <DependsOnNETStandard>false</DependsOnNETStandard>
    </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
